# This git repository is rooted at the Windows home directory, so by default
# every personal file under C:\Users\palan is a candidate for `git add`.
# That includes .ssh private keys, .claude.json credentials, AppData, browser
# profiles and NTUSER.DAT -- none of which belong in a public repository.
#
# So: ignore everything, then re-admit only this repo's project folder --
# sop-checker has its own repository now. Nothing at the top level is ever
# staged unless it is added to the allow-list below, which makes
# `git add -A` from this directory safe instead of catastrophic.

/*

!/.gitignore
!/legal-rag/
